---
import SourceLink from '../components/SourceLink.astro';
import StatusTag from '../components/StatusTag.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getLatestPublishedRecord } from '../lib/catalog';
import {
  importCheckoutReplayCommand,
  importConsumerSourceUrl,
  importImplementationCommit,
  importPolicySourceUrl,
} from '../lib/import-replay';
import { artifactUrl, sourceUrl, registry } from '../lib/modules';
import discovery from '../../public/.well-known/mathgraph.json';

const sourcePublished = await getLatestPublishedRecord('mg-l4yaml-source-check-20261010');
const resolvePublished = await getLatestPublishedRecord('mg-living-warrant-openai-jpl-20261010');
const { record } = sourcePublished;
const { entry: resolveEntry } = resolvePublished;
const resolveOfflineRoot = `https://mathgraph.org/evidence/${resolveEntry.id}/offline`;
const resolveConsumerSha256 = '27a9be606040cc94a47c9b903dfc1cb24a86cbbc4e05ce71040c6c3d6e8d527b';
const resolvePolicySha256 = '09e8d5ba97bca126a81dfe0fcbd5d57f3915ffe71402a497ece4d5e6117f2b4a';
const typescriptConsumerSha256 = 'e7360df24b2fd0900c8ea88ccb1689163cec73a6c2e2347e4ab2b23b4d01bc2e';
const request = {
  record_id: record.id,
  source_commit: record.source.commit,
  external_suite_commit: record.source.external_suite_commit,
  goal: 'finite_parser_acceptance',
};
const response = {
  authority: 'PINNED_SOURCE_LEAN_GUARDS',
  evidence: ['https://github.com/metalogiclabs/mathgraph/actions/runs/38020008793'],
  record_id: record.id,
  record_sha256: record.content_sha256,
  scope: '48 pinned external YAML cases plus 4 Lean guard controls',
  status: 'WARRANTED_BOUNDED',
  truth_promotion: false,
  verified: { extra_controls: 4, matched: 48, total: 48 },
  whole_language_validity: 'UNKNOWN',
};
const permanentRecordUrl = `https://mathgraph.org/records/${record.id}/v1/`;
const badgeUrl = `https://mathgraph.org/v1/badges/${record.id}.svg`;
const badgeMarkdown = `[![MathGraph: warranted — bounded](${badgeUrl})](${permanentRecordUrl})`;
const badgeHtml = `<a href="${permanentRecordUrl}"><img src="${badgeUrl}" alt="MathGraph: warranted — bounded"></a>`;
const sourceCatalogue = discovery.source_catalogue;
---

<BaseLayout title="MathGraph Developers — Consume exact evidence" description="Use the current immutable MathGraph record, reproduce its evidence, and understand the exact source-bound resolver contract." currentPath="/developers/">
  <header class="section section--compact">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="eyebrow">Developers</div>
      <h1>Consume the records. Keep their boundaries.</h1>
      <p class="lede">MathGraph publishes immutable static evidence and independently runnable consumers. Record 001 supports exact source-scope matching; record 002 supports bounded offline dependency replay. The qualified local resolver is not publicly deployed.</p>
      <p>Lean/Mathlib entry points: <a href="/explore/?q=Real.rpow">inspect a real declaration</a> · <a href="/records/mg-l4yaml-source-check-20261010/">see the pinned public JPL case</a> · <a href="#source-catalogue">replay the catalogue contract offline</a>. Source-indexed structural relations are not proof dependencies, and historical receipt validation does not rerun the original Lean checker.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell page-grid">
      <aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <strong>On this page</strong>
        <a href="#quickstart">Quickstart</a>
        <a href="#source-catalogue">Source catalogue</a>
        <a href="#modules">Local modules</a>
        <a href="#interoperability">Interoperability</a>
        <a href="#offline-replay">Offline replay</a>
        <a href="#typescript-consumer">TypeScript consumer</a>
        <a href="#discovery">Discovery</a>
        <a href="#embed">Scoped badge</a>
        <a href="#format">Record format</a>
        <a href="#resolver">Resolver</a>
        <a href="#reproduce">Reproduce</a>
        <a href="#compatibility">Compatibility</a>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <section id="quickstart">
          <div class="eyebrow">Quickstart</div>
          <h2>Replay the exact source-check record</h2>
          <p>The importer is available on <code>main</code>, but this historical replay deliberately detaches at exact implementation commit <code>{importImplementationCommit}</code>. The release checkout exercises its current local import consumer and policy in CI; the command below preserves the original implementation boundary. No hosted resolver or MCP service is involved.</p>
          <div class="code-block"><div class="code-label">Shell · Python 3.11+</div><pre tabindex="0"><code>{importCheckoutReplayCommand}</code></pre></div>
          <p><a href={importConsumerSourceUrl}>Inspect the pinned independent consumer ↗</a> · <a href={importPolicySourceUrl}>Inspect the separately reviewed pinned policy ↗</a></p>
          <p>The trust-policy digest in the command must be obtained through a channel trusted separately from the evidence and policy bytes. This historical replay does not run the original proof, kernel, or source suite; current applicability remains <code>UNKNOWN</code>.</p>
          <h3>Fetch the public evidence bytes separately</h3>
          <div class="code-block"><div class="code-label">Shell</div><pre tabindex="0"><code>curl --fail --silent \
  https://mathgraph.org/evidence/{record.id}/record.json \
  -o record.json

sha256sum record.json</code></pre></div>
          <p>The transport-file hash is distinct from the record’s canonical content digest. Consumers should validate the schema, exact record ID, <code>content_sha256</code>, source commits, and requested scope before using the result.</p>
          <SourceLink href={`/evidence/${record.id}/record.json`} label="Open record JSON" meta={`${record.id} · immutable snapshot`} />
        </section>

        <section id="source-catalogue">
          <div class="eyebrow">Source catalogue · Python</div>
          <h2>Replay the pinned Mathlib source index offline.</h2>
          <p>At exact retrieval snapshot <code>{sourceCatalogue.repository_snapshot_commit}</code>, this standard-library consumer validates the canonical manifest, manifest-listed shards, search derivation, source identities, structural relation meanings, endpoint closure, counts, and publication budgets. The exact public trust policy identifies producer <code>{sourceCatalogue.qualification.public_bundle.producer_commit}</code> and qualification wrapper <code>{sourceCatalogue.qualification.public_bundle.wrapper_commit}</code>; its same-owner independent qualification run is <a href={sourceCatalogue.qualification.public_bundle.run_url}>public on GitHub Actions ↗</a>.</p>
          <p>The bundle was committed at <code>{sourceCatalogue.qualification.publication_commit}</code>. A later <a href={sourceCatalogue.qualification.later_regeneration.run_url}>catalogue regeneration run ↗</a> at <code>{sourceCatalogue.qualification.later_regeneration.commit}</code> reproduced the catalogue with a run-specific policy. It did <strong>not</strong> replay the exact public trust-policy bytes; these are distinct provenance scopes.</p>
          <div class="code-block" data-source-catalogue-command><div class="code-label">Exact retrieval snapshot · Python 3</div><pre tabindex="0"><code>git checkout --detach {sourceCatalogue.repository_snapshot_commit}

python3 -I -S -B conformance/source_catalogue_v1/consumer.py \
  --catalogue-root website/public/catalogues/mathlib/v4.34.1 \
  --policy conformance/source_catalogue_v1/trust-policy.json \
  --policy-sha256 {sourceCatalogue.artifacts.trust_policy.sha256} \
  --audit-imports</code></pre></div>
          <div class="code-block"><div class="code-label">Exact result</div><pre tabindex="0"><code>{JSON.stringify(sourceCatalogue.result)}</code></pre></div>
          <p>Manifest SHA-256: <code>{sourceCatalogue.artifacts.manifest.sha256}</code>. Consumer SHA-256: <code>{sourceCatalogue.artifacts.consumer.sha256}</code>.</p>
          <p>The consumer imports neither the producer implementation nor the MathGraph protocol package. It does not fetch upstream source, run Lean, prove declarations, check current applicability, or authorize action. <code>SOURCE_INDEXED</code> means the pinned source structure passed this finite publication contract; independent proof verification remains <code>NOT_CHECKED</code>.</p>
          <div class="source-stack">
            <SourceLink href={sourceCatalogue.artifacts.manifest.url} label="Pinned source catalogue manifest" meta={`SHA-256 ${sourceCatalogue.artifacts.manifest.sha256}`} />
            <SourceLink href={sourceCatalogue.artifacts.consumer.url} label="Independent standard-library consumer" meta={`SHA-256 ${sourceCatalogue.artifacts.consumer.sha256}`} />
            <SourceLink href={sourceCatalogue.artifacts.trust_policy.url} label="Separately pinned trust policy" meta={`SHA-256 ${sourceCatalogue.artifacts.trust_policy.sha256}`} />
            <SourceLink href={sourceCatalogue.artifacts.readme.url} label="Replay and trust-boundary README" meta="Static source · no hosted endpoint" />
          </div>
          <p>A same-origin digest detects changed bytes only relative to a trusted pin. Obtain the manifest and policy pins through an independently chosen channel; a Git repository identity is itself a trust-policy choice and is not mathematical truth.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="modules">
          <h2>Use the modular contracts locally.</h2>
          <p><a href="/discover/">Discover</a> exposes a deterministic advisory request/result contract. <a href="/develop/">Develop</a> publishes one exact finite replay. The <a href="/capabilities/">Capabilities registry</a> separates the qualified finite entry from experimental candidates. Hosted services remain <code>NOT_DEPLOYED</code>; these commands run from a repository checkout.</p>
          <div class="code-block"><div class="code-label">Local CLI · Python standard library</div><pre tabindex="0"><code>python3 -I -S scripts/mathgraph_discover_v1.py --request conformance/discover_v1/fixtures/request.json

python3 -I -S scripts/mathgraph_capability_v1.py --contract conformance/capability_v1/fixtures/capability-contract.json

python3 -I -S conformance/capability_v1/consumer.py \
  --fixture conformance/capability_v1/fixtures/finite-representation-refinement-v1.json \
  --contract conformance/capability_v1/fixtures/capability-contract.json \
  --policy conformance/capability_v1/trust-policy.json \
  --policy-sha256 {registry.qualified_entries[0].trust_policy.sha256}</code></pre></div>
          <p>The Discover example is <code>PARTIAL</code>, advisory-only, with verification <code>NOT_CHECKED</code> and <code>FULL_REPLAY_UNAVAILABLE</code>. Attention allocates work; it is not truth confidence.</p>
          <p>The general descriptor evaluator returns <code>UNKNOWN</code>, including when its process exits 0. Only the separate exact finite replay produces <code>QUALIFIED_BOUNDED</code>. Obtain the consumer and policy pins through a separately trusted channel before executing; same-origin hashes do not authenticate their publisher.</p>
          <p><a href="/schemas/discover-request-v1.schema.json">Discover request</a> · <a href="/schemas/discover-result-v1.schema.json">Discover result</a> · <a href="/schemas/capability-contract-v1.schema.json">Capability descriptor</a> · <a href="/schemas/capability-evaluation-v1.schema.json">Evaluation</a> · <a href="/schemas/capability-registry-v1.schema.json">Registry schema</a></p>
          <p><a href={sourceUrl('conformance/capability_v1/README.md')}>Finite consumer and isolated replay instructions ↗</a></p>
        </section>

        <section id="interoperability">
          <h2>Unsigned external correspondence.</h2>
          <p>The local in-toto adapter provides <strong>unsigned correspondence only</strong> while binding the exact capability artifact bytes, claim, assumptions, and evidence. Its checked result is correspondence only: signature <code>UNSIGNED</code>; authenticity, signer policy, transparency, and freshness <code>NOT_CHECKED</code>; qualification and current applicability <code>UNKNOWN</code>; action authorization <code>NONE</code>.</p>
          <p>The caller selects the expected artifact pin independently. A wrapper never imports the finite contract’s qualification. Sigstore, SCITT, and RATS integrations remain deferred; no signing or transparency verification is implemented here.</p>
          <p><a href={artifactUrl('conformance/interoperability_v1/statement.json')}>Exact in-toto statement</a> · <a href="/schemas/external-binding-v1.schema.json">Binding schema</a> · <a href={sourceUrl('docs/external_interoperability_v1.md')}>Local correspondence contract ↗</a></p>
        </section>

        <section id="offline-replay">
          <div class="eyebrow">Resolve · Python</div>
          <h2>Replay record 002 without MathGraph.org</h2>
          <p>Acquire these three static inputs first. The replay itself imports only the Python standard library and needs no MathGraph package, service, LLM, or network connection. The trust-policy digest must come from a channel you trust separately from the downloaded policy.</p>
          <p>The <a href="/schemas/resolve-bundle-v1.schema.json">Resolve bundle schema</a> and <a href="/schemas/resolve-trust-policy-v1.schema.json">Resolve trust-policy schema</a> describe the published transport structure. These schemas do not authenticate records or replace the separately pinned trust policy and semantic replay.</p>
          <div class="code-block"><div class="code-label">Shell · Python 3.11+</div><pre tabindex="0"><code>mkdir mathgraph-resolve-v1
cd mathgraph-resolve-v1
curl --fail --remote-name {resolveOfflineRoot}/consumer.py
curl --fail --remote-name {resolveOfflineRoot}/bundle.json
curl --fail --remote-name {resolveOfflineRoot}/trust-policy.json

python3 -I -S -c 'import sys; from hashlib import sha256; from pathlib import Path; expected="{resolveConsumerSha256}"; actual=sha256(Path("consumer.py").read_bytes()).hexdigest(); sys.exit(None if actual == expected else "consumer.py SHA-256 mismatch: "+actual)'
python3 -I -S -c 'import sys; from hashlib import sha256; from pathlib import Path; expected="{resolvePolicySha256}"; actual=sha256(Path("trust-policy.json").read_bytes()).hexdigest(); sys.exit(None if actual == expected else "trust-policy.json SHA-256 mismatch: "+actual)'

python3 -I -S consumer.py \
  --bundle bundle.json \
  --policy trust-policy.json \
  --policy-sha256 {resolvePolicySha256}</code></pre></div>
          <p><strong>Trust the executable first.</strong> Verify the independently obtained consumer and policy pins before execution. Hashes copied only from the same origin as the files provide integrity comparison, not publisher authenticity.</p>
          <p>The deterministic report recomputes the seven historical results. It does not accept the snapshot’s reported statuses as resolution authority, rerun the original JPL Lean proof, establish current applicability, or authorize an action.</p>
          <div class="source-stack">
            <SourceLink href={`${resolveOfflineRoot}/consumer.py`} label="Download consumer.py" meta="Exact qualified standard-library consumer" />
            <SourceLink href={`${resolveOfflineRoot}/bundle.json`} label="Download bundle.json" meta="Immutable source-pinned bundle" />
            <SourceLink href={`${resolveOfflineRoot}/trust-policy.json`} label="Download trust-policy.json" meta={`Expected SHA-256 ${resolvePolicySha256}`} />
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="typescript-consumer">
          <div class="eyebrow">Resolve · TypeScript</div>
          <h2>Check the published static interface over HTTP</h2>
          <div class="code-block"><div class="code-label">Shell · Node 24</div><pre tabindex="0"><code>curl --fail \
  https://mathgraph.org/examples/resolve-consumer-v1.ts \
  -o resolve-consumer-v1.ts

python3 -I -S -c 'import sys; from hashlib import sha256; from pathlib import Path; expected="{typescriptConsumerSha256}"; actual=sha256(Path("resolve-consumer-v1.ts").read_bytes()).hexdigest(); sys.exit(None if actual == expected else "resolve-consumer-v1.ts SHA-256 mismatch: "+actual)'

node resolve-consumer-v1.ts https://mathgraph.org</code></pre></div>
          <p>The TypeScript reference is an HTTP client, not an offline replay. It accepts one origin, fetches only fixed documented paths, validates independently compiled-in authority pins, and recomputes the bounded historical closure. It does not provide a public execution endpoint.</p>
          <p>The exact static path is declared as <code>text/plain; charset=utf-8</code> for direct inspection while the global <code>nosniff</code> protection remains enabled. The source stays Node-oriented TypeScript; it is not browser JavaScript, proof code, or a resolver endpoint.</p>
          <SourceLink href="/examples/resolve-consumer-v1.ts" label="Open TypeScript reference consumer" meta="Local client · Node 24" />
        </section>

        <section id="format">
          <h2>Current public record format</h2>
          <p><code>mathgraph.public-consequence-record.v1</code> separates admission state from finite observations, formal proof replay, fidelity, generalization, current requalification, and source-specific discrepancies.</p>
          <div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Consumer meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
            <tr><td><code>id</code></td><td>Stable identifier: <code>{record.id}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>content_sha256</code></td><td>Canonical record digest: <code>{record.content_sha256}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>source.commit</code></td><td>Original source pin: <code>{record.source.commit}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>source.external_suite_commit</code></td><td>External suite pin: <code>{record.source.external_suite_commit}</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>axes</code></td><td>Independent observations and explicit unknowns; no global truth promotion.</td></tr>
          </tbody></table></div>
        </section>

        <section id="discovery">
          <h2>Machine discovery and permanent versions</h2>
          <p>Agents begin with <a href="/llms.txt"><code>/llms.txt</code></a> or the versioned <a href="/.well-known/mathgraph.json"><code>/.well-known/mathgraph.json</code></a> discovery manifest, then fetch the short-lived <a href="/records/index.json">record index</a>. Record a local <code>fetched_at</code> time and re-fetch before <code>max_age_seconds</code> elapse; <code>generated_at</code> is the publication time, not a live response timestamp.</p>
          <p>The stable human route for this snapshot is <a href={`/records/${record.id}/v1/`}><code>/records/{record.id}/v1/</code></a>. Its qualified evidence JSON stays immutable. Citation, lifecycle presentation, and discovery metadata live in a separately versioned <a href={`/records/${record.id}/v1/metadata.json`}>presentation sidecar</a> with visible history; changing that sidecar does not requalify the evidence.</p>
          <p>The <a href="/protocol/profiles/lean/">Lean evidence profile</a> is a proposed draft, not a currently implemented record type.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="embed">
          <h2>Scoped badge embed</h2>
          <p>The existing badge describes only the pinned finite observation and links to the permanent V1 boundary. It is not a universal truth badge, a statement-fidelity certificate, or an endorsement mark.</p>
          <div class="code-block"><div class="code-label">Markdown</div><pre tabindex="0"><code>{badgeMarkdown}</code></pre></div>
          <div class="code-block"><div class="code-label">HTML</div><pre tabindex="0"><code>{badgeHtml}</code></pre></div>
          <p><a href={`/v1/badges/${record.id}.svg`}>Open the scoped status SVG →</a></p>
        </section>

        <section id="resolver">
          <h2>Exact source-bound resolver</h2>
          <p>The qualified release defines <code>POST /v1/resolve</code> as a localhost read-only preview. It accepts only exact pins and a supported goal. It has strict JSON, content-type, method, and request-size checks. The OpenAPI file is a reproducible contract, not evidence of a hosted service.</p>
          <div class="code-block"><div class="code-label">Request JSON</div><pre tabindex="0"><code>{JSON.stringify(request, null, 2)}</code></pre></div>
          <div class="code-block"><div class="code-label">Qualified response</div><pre tabindex="0"><code>{JSON.stringify(response, null, 2)}</code></pre></div>
          <p><StatusTag label="WARRANTED_BOUNDED" tone="bounded" /> is returned only for the exact record, both exact source pins, and the supported finite agreement goal. An incorrect pin, unsupported goal, or unknown version returns <StatusTag label="UNKNOWN" tone="unknown" /> or an explicit request error; it never inherits a warrant.</p>
          <SourceLink href={`/evidence/${record.id}/openapi.preview.json`} label="OpenAPI preview contract" meta="Qualified local resolver · no public endpoint" />
          <div class="callout callout--unknown"><StatusTag label="Deployment boundary" tone="unknown" /><p>Public resolver: <code>NOT_DEPLOYED</code>. MCP: <code>NOT_DEPLOYED</code>. These static consumers do not expose a service, accept arbitrary proof code, or fetch visitor-supplied URLs.</p></div>
        </section>

        <section id="reproduce">
          <h2>Reproduce the qualification</h2>
          <div class="code-block"><div class="code-label">Python</div><pre tabindex="0"><code>export MATHGRAPH_V1_EVIDENCE_ZIP=/path/to/l4yaml-v1.zip
export MATHGRAPH_V2_EVIDENCE_ZIP=/path/to/l4yaml-v2.zip
python3 -m unittest discover \
  -s tests -p test_mathgraph_public_evidence_v1.py -v</code></pre></div>
          <p>The 13-test gate validates archive digests, source pins, the publication integrity gate, tamper rejection, negative lineage, resolver method and input limits, fail-closed unknowns, and agreement between human and machine-readable outputs.</p>
          <div class="source-stack">
            <SourceLink href="https://github.com/metalogiclabs/mathgraph/tree/7c1fd9be80966ece12ba455375319961194ae7f4" label="Qualified release source" meta="commit 7c1fd9b" />
            <SourceLink href="https://github.com/metalogiclabs/mathgraph/actions/runs/38021785401" label="Qualification run" meta="13/13 isolated release tests" />
            <SourceLink href="https://github.com/metalogiclabs/mathgraph/actions/runs/38020008793" label="Decoded-source replay" meta="48 cases + 4 controls" />
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="compatibility">
          <h2>Versioning and compatibility</h2>
          <p>Consumers should treat schema names, record IDs, content digests, and source pins as exact. Unknown versions or fields must be retained where possible and must not be interpreted as known types. No endpoint currently promises automatic requalification, arbitrary proof execution, URL fetching, or a universal truth verdict.</p>
          <div class="callout callout--unknown"><StatusTag label="Current limit" tone="unknown" /><p>The record establishes finite pinned observations and replayed source-scoped proof evidence. Whole-language YAML correctness, natural-language fidelity, and all newer source revisions remain <code>UNKNOWN</code>.</p></div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
